{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Scope placement changes answers: node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e puts offering in Scope; node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5, node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5, node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 put promotional linkage in Scope. False conditions return OUT_OF_SCOPE rather than the typed negative answer (or satisfaction of the selected compliance control). These may be intended applicability boundaries, but that interpretation remains unresolved.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional connection with an existential gift component. Require the same component to bear the relevant promotional connection; otherwise unrelated components could jointly produce an unsupported prohibition.",
    "Unit db43e253bea18.u0.2 defines distributors in the context of SFC-authorised funds, while u13.2987 describes a specific investment product or product type. Resolve broader distributor wording in some candidates and node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f's narrower specific-fund wording against that distinction before asserting equivalence.",
    "Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 and the answer to question 1 of the SFC's 30 September 2010 FAQs, referenced in footnote 3, are not supplied as external authorities. Can their applicable texts be supplied to check qualifications and substantive gift classifications? No dependency IDs are available.",
    "The source says guaranteed returns and incentives may be gifts. Their classification must remain individually assessed; neither incentive status nor the presence of a separate discount determines the result for another component.",
    "A discount exception or TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT result addresses only the selected gift control. It does not grant permission under section 103, paragraph 2.3 or other applicable requirements.",
    "The supplied source does not establish the candidates' stated operative time interval. Applicable versions and dates remain unresolved.",
    "Node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b's categorical statements about funding and fulfilment independence extend beyond the express source wording. Offering, rather than payment, is the stated trigger, but attribution in third-party arrangements still requires assessment."
  ],
